"Jeju"}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6","children":"Major Cities"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5","children":[["$","$La","seoul",{"city":{"slug":"seoul","name":"Seoul","tagline":"Where tradition meets neon","description":"South Korea's sprawling capital is a city of contrasts — ancient palaces sit beneath glass skyscrapers, street food alleys wind past Michelin-starred restaurants, and quiet temple grounds border the loudest nightlife districts in Asia.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617469767053-d3b523a0b982?w=1200&q=80","regionSlug":"seoul-metropolitan","lat":37.5665,"lng":126.978,"bestFor":["nightlife","food","shopping","culture"]}}],["$","$La","busan",{"city":{"slug":"busan","name":"Busan","tagline":"Beaches, temples and seafood","description":"South Korea's second city hugs the southeastern coastline with golden beaches, dramatic cliffside temples, and the freshest seafood you'll find anywhere in the country.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596478573744-0d1af41d9c09?w=1200&q=80","regionSlug":"busan-metropolitan","lat":35.1796,"lng":129.0756,"bestFor":["beaches","food","temples"]}}],["$","$La","incheon",{"city":{"slug":"incheon","name":"Incheon","tagline":"Gateway to Korea","description":"More than just an airport city — Incheon has Chinatown, Art Deco architecture, island ferries and a waterfront that's reinventing itself as a cultural hub.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548115184-bc6544d06a58?w=1200&q=80","regionSlug":"incheon-metropolitan","bestFor":["transport","culture","food"]}}],["$","$La","daegu",{"city":{"slug":"daegu","name":"Daegu","tagline":"The hot and vibrant heart","description":"Korea's fourth-largest city is known for its searing summers, textile markets, excellent food scene and growing cafe culture.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573057284059-827a26b093f4?w=1200&q=80","regionSlug":"daegu-metropolitan","bestFor":["food","shopping","culture"]}}],["$","$La","daejeon",{"city":{"slug":"daejeon","name":"Daejeon","tagline":"Science and saunas","description":"Korea's science capital sits in the centre of the country. Hot springs, a massive expo park and easy access to the mountains of South Chungcheong make it a worthy stop.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517154421773-0529f29ea451?w=1200&q=80","regionSlug":"daejeon-metropolitan","bestFor":["nature","science","hot-springs"]}}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6","children":"Top Itineraries"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5","children":[["$","$L7","3-days-in-seoul",{"href":"/itineraries/3-days-in-seoul","className":"group block overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-card transition-all duration-240","style":{"boxShadow":"var(--shadow-card)"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"aspect-[3/2] overflow-hidden","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617469767053-d3b523a0b982?w=1200&q=80","alt":"3 Days In Seoul","width":800,"height":533,"className":"w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 sm:p-5","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1.5","children":[3," Days"]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-foreground","children":"3 Days In Seoul"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1.5 line-clamp-2","children":"The essential Seoul itinerary — palaces, street food, nightlife and neighbourhood exploration packed into three unforgettable days."}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6","children":"Popular Guides"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5","children":[["$","$Lb","best-bars-hongdae",{"guide":{"slug":"best-bars-hongdae","title":"Best Bars In Hongdae","city":"seoul","category":"nightlife","neighbourhood":"Hongdae","neighbourhoodSlug":"hongdae","priceRange":"₩₩ – ₩₩₩","nearestMetro":"Hongik University (Line 2)","openingHours":"6 PM – 3 AM","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1514933651103-005eec06c04b?w=1200&q=80","summary":"From craft cocktails to soju dives — the definitive Hongdae bar guide.","intro":"Hongdae's bar scene is as eclectic as the neighbourhood itself. Graffiti-walled dives sit next to sleek cocktail lounges, and on any given night the energy spills from the venues onto the streets. Here are the spots worth your time.","venues":[{"name":"Café Abyss","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572116469696-31de0f17cc34?w=600&q=80","description":"A moody, candlelit cocktail bar with an extensive whisky list and jazz playing low in the background. The bartenders here are serious about their craft.","address":"32-8 Wausan-ro 21-gil, Mapo-gu","tip":"Ask for the off-menu 'Midnight Seoul' cocktail — it's their signature and it's incredible.","priceLevel":"₩₩₩"},{"name":"Thursday Party","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566417713940-fe7c737a9ef2?w=600&q=80","description":"The quintessential Hongdae dive bar. Cheap soju towers, loud music, and a crowd that's always up for a good time. Don't come here for quiet conversation.","address":"19-3 Wausan-ro 29na-gil, Mapo-gu","tip":"Thursday nights are obviously the busiest — go Wednesday for the same vibe with more space.","priceLevel":"₩"},{"name":"Vault 82","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1525268323446-0505b6fe7778?w=600&q=80","description":"A speakeasy-style bar hidden behind an unmarked door. The cocktail menu changes seasonally and the interior feels like stepping into a 1920s bank vault.","address":"82 Eoulmadang-ro, Mapo-gu","tip":"Ring the doorbell and wait — the entrance is intentionally hard to find. Look for the brass plate.","priceLevel":"₩₩₩"}],"relatedSlugs":["nightlife-itaewon","best-street-food-myeongdong"],"tags":["Bars","Cocktails","Nightlife"],"authorSlug":"james-jeong","updatedDate":"2026-03-10","contentType":"guide"}}],["$","$Lb","nightlife-itaewon",{"guide":{"slug":"nightlife-itaewon","title":"Itaewon After Dark","city":"seoul","category":"nightlife","neighbourhood":"Itaewon","neighbourhoodSlug":"itaewon","priceRange":"₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩","nearestMetro":"Itaewon (Line 6)","openingHours":"8 PM – 5 AM","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519608487953-e999c86e7455?w=1200&q=80","summary":"Seoul's most international nightlife district — rooftop bars, clubs and late-night eats.","intro":"Itaewon has always been Seoul's most cosmopolitan neighbourhood, and its nightlife reflects that. From rooftop cocktail bars overlooking the city to underground clubs playing everything from techno to K-pop, this is where Seoul stays up latest.","venues":[{"name":"Southside Parlor","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470337458703-46ad1756a187?w=600&q=80","description":"A Southern-inspired whisky bar that feels like it was teleported from Nashville. Great bourbon selection and surprisingly good fried chicken.","address":"218 Noksapyeong-daero, Yongsan-gu","tip":"The upstairs terrace opens in spring and summer — get there early to grab a seat.","priceLevel":"₩₩₩"}],"relatedSlugs":["best-bars-hongdae"],"tags":["Clubs","Rooftop Bars","Late Night"],"authorSlug":"james-jeong","updatedDate":"2026-03-08","contentType":"guide"}}],["$","$Lb","best-street-food-myeongdong",{"guide":{"slug":"best-street-food-myeongdong","title":"Best Street Food In Myeongdong","city":"seoul","category":"food","neighbourhood":"Myeongdong","neighbourhoodSlug":"myeongdong","priceRange":"₩","nearestMetro":"Myeongdong (Line 4)","openingHours":"11 AM – 10 PM","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498654896293-37aacf113fd9?w=1200&q=80","summary":"Tteokbokki, hotteok, tornado potatoes — everything you need to eat on Myeongdong's food streets.","intro":"Myeongdong's main streets transform into an open-air food market every afternoon. Vendors line both sides selling everything from freshly grilled skewers to towering soft-serve ice cream. Come hungry.","venues":[{"name":"Myeongdong Kyoja","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590301157890-4810ed352733?w=600&q=80","description":"A Myeongdong institution serving handmade kalguksu (knife-cut noodles) since 1966. The broth is rich and deeply savoury.","address":"29 Myeongdong 10-gil, Jung-gu","tip":"There's always a queue but it moves fast. The mandu (dumplings) are a must-order alongside the noodles.","priceLevel":"₩"}],"relatedSlugs":["best-bars-hongdae","cafes-gangnam"],"tags":["Street Food","Budget","Must Try"],"authorSlug":"mina-park","updatedDate":"2026-02-28","contentType":"guide"}}],["$","$Lb","cafes-gangnam",{"guide":{"slug":"cafes-gangnam","title":"Best Cafes In Gangnam","city":"seoul","category":"food","neighbourhood":"Gangnam","neighbourhoodSlug":"gangnam","priceRange":"₩₩","nearestMetro":"Gangnam (Line 2)","openingHours":"9 AM – 10 PM","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559305616-3f99cd43e353?w=1200&q=80","summary":"Design-forward coffee shops and hidden gems south of the river.","intro":"Gangnam's cafe scene is all about aesthetics and quality. Multi-storey minimalist spaces, rooftop gardens, and some of Seoul's best specialty coffee — these are the ones worth crossing the river for.","venues":[{"name":"Fritz Coffee","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?w=600&q=80","description":"A beloved Seoul roastery with a cosy industrial interior and pastries baked fresh on-site. Their hand-drip coffee is consistently excellent.","address":"17 Dosan-daero 15-gil, Gangnam-gu","tip":"Try the einspänner — their version with house-made whipped cream is the best in Seoul.","priceLevel":"₩₩"}],"relatedSlugs":["best-street-food-myeongdong"],"tags":["Coffee","Design","Brunch"],"authorSlug":"mina-park","updatedDate":"2026-03-05","contentType":"guide"}}],["$","$Lb","hiking-bukhansan",{"guide":{"slug":"hiking-bukhansan","title":"Hiking Bukhansan National Park","city":"seoul","category":"things-to-do","neighbourhood":"Jongno","neighbourhoodSlug":"jamsil","priceRange":"Free","nearestMetro":"Gupabal (Line 3)","openingHours":"Sunrise – Sunset","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1200&q=80","summary":"Granite peaks and temple trails on the northern edge of Seoul.","intro":"Bukhansan is the dramatic granite mountain visible from almost anywhere in northern Seoul. Multiple trails wind through forests and past Buddhist temples to summit ridges with panoramic city views. It's one of the most visited national parks in the world — for good reason.","venues":[{"name":"Baegundae Peak Trail","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551632811-561732d1e306?w=600&q=80","description":"The most popular trail to Bukhansan's highest point (836m). The final section involves steel cables and rock scrambling — exhilarating but not for the faint-hearted.","address":"Bukhansan National Park, Gangbuk-gu","tip":"Start before 7 AM on weekends to beat the crowds. Bring gloves for the cable section.","priceLevel":"Free"}],"relatedSlugs":["best-street-food-myeongdong"],"tags":["Hiking","Nature","Free"],"authorSlug":"mina-park","updatedDate":"2026-02-20","contentType":"guide"}}],["$","$Lb","haeundae-beach-guide",{"guide":{"slug":"haeundae-beach-guide","title":"Haeundae Beach Guide","city":"busan","category":"things-to-do","neighbourhood":"Haeundae","neighbourhoodSlug":"haeundae","priceRange":"₩ – ₩₩","nearestMetro":"Haeundae (Line 2)","openingHours":"All day","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573057284059-827a26b093f4?w=1200&q=80","summary":"Everything you need to know about Busan's most famous beach.","intro":"Haeundae is the beach you've seen in every Korean drama. A wide crescent of sand backed by high-rises, it's the epicentre of Busan's summer scene. But there's more to it than sunbathing — the surrounding area is packed with seafood restaurants, markets, and cliff walks.","venues":[{"name":"Haeundae Traditional Market","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1567521464027-f127ff144326?w=600&q=80","description":"A bustling covered market a few blocks from the beach. Fresh seafood, dried fish, street snacks and local produce at great prices.","address":"Gunam-ro 41beon-gil, Haeundae-gu","tip":"Head to the second floor for some of the best (and cheapest) raw fish sets in Busan.","priceLevel":"₩"}],"relatedSlugs":[],"tags":["Beach","Seafood","Summer"],"authorSlug":"mina-park","updatedDate":"2026-03-12","contentType":"guide"}}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6","children":"Travel Tips"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4","children":[["$","$L7","seoul-subway-guide",{"href":"/travel-tips/seoul-subway-guide","className":"flex items-center gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-card hover:bg-secondary/50 transition-colors","style":{"boxShadow":"var(--shadow-card)"},"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617469767053-d3b523a0b982?w=1200&q=80","alt":"","width":56,"height":56,"className":"w-14 h-14 rounded-lg object-cover","loading":"lazy"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground","children":"How To Use The Seoul Subway"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-0.5 line-clamp-1","children":"Everything you need to know about navigating Seoul's metro system — apps, etiquette and tips."}]]}]]}],["$","$L7","incheon-airport-to-seoul",{"href":